# Identity, governance, authorization

Use `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md` to locate AUTH contracts, Phase 010 Group 03, and Implementation 002.

Preserve directly:

- Entity Identity ≠ source name/path/ID;
- rename continuity requires evidence; delete/recreate does not imply identity;
- Principal authentication/binding ≠ Capability Authorization;
- Monitoring Scope ≠ Assertion Authority ≠ Capability Authorization;
- Responsibility Assignment/title/admin/repository ownership ≠ Assertion Authority;
- source assertion ≠ authoritative assertion; recency/count/ingestion order are not authority precedence;
- evidence sufficiency ≠ authority ≠ authorization ≠ enforcement/action;
- current visibility/disclosure permission does not rewrite historical truth or retained communication;
- unknown/conflicting/unavailable authorization is not invented allow/deny;
- tenant/environment boundaries must remain explicit.

Authority and authorization decisions that materially affect outputs/actions retain rule/version/principal/time provenance.
